WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Friday,

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.360
the twentieth of November.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.480
This episode is written and read with AI.

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.000
The International Energy Agency says
the Middle East war has taken two

5
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.467
point eight billion barrels
of oil off global supply,

6
00:00:15.493 --> 00:00:19.680
and that there's no route back to the
energy world as it was before Hormuz.

7
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.680
Meanwhile, the EU has given oil and
gas importers two more years before

8
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.840
its methane rules bite. And another
tanker was struck in the strait overnight.

9
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.800
On the markets. Brent traded at
ninety-two dollars a barrel on Thursday

10
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.360
morning, according to OilPrice dot com.

11
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.440
West Texas Intermediate was
at eighty-three dollars.

12
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.240
In Europe, gas storage stood at
sixty-nine point eight percent full on

13
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.640
the eighteenth of November, down
about a tenth of a point on the day,

14
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.960
according to Gas Infrastructure Europe.

15
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.427
The International Energy Agency's World
Energy Outlook came out on Thursday.

16
00:00:52.453 --> 00:00:56.080
It estimates the war has removed two
point eight billion barrels of oil

17
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.840
from global supply, along with sixty
billion cubic metres of natural

18
00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.480
gas. The agency finds no credible
pathway back to the system that existed

19
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.120
before the crisis.

20
00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.080
It sketches two directions.

21
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.387
If shipping risk drags on,
buyers build around the strait,

22
00:01:11.413 --> 00:01:14.320
and the oil that needs to pass
through Hormuz could fall from twenty

23
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.480
million barrels a day to under
two million by twenty thirty-five.

24
00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.760
A clear resolution instead points
to a buyer's market for oil and gas.

25
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.333
Under the agency's
current-policies scenario,

26
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.840
demand for both keeps growing either way.

27
00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.440
The catch is that this
is a long-range outlook,

28
00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.360
not a read on today's flows.

29
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.600
The near-term numbers point the other way.

30
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.400
According to the EIA, oil shipments
through Middle East chokepoints rose

31
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.880
nineteen percent in the third quarter.

32
00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.200
Staying in the Gulf, there's
been another strike on a tanker.

33
00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:48.080
The UK Maritime Trade Operations
centre issued a fresh warning overnight

34
00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.680
Wednesday after reports that an
unidentified tanker was hit in the strait.

35
00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.400
That comes after a vessel from ADNOC
Logistics and Services was attacked

36
00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.960
on Tuesday. Splash twenty-four seven
counts two seafarers missing and

37
00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.173
more than a dozen injured this week.

38
00:02:03.227 --> 00:02:05.320
What isn't known yet is the tanker's name,

39
00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.960
its owner, or how badly it was damaged.

40
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.400
None of that is in the reports so far.

41
00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.960
gCaptain describes Iran's attacks
on tankers as intensifying.

42
00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.520
Prices barely reacted. Rigzone describes
crude swinging as Iran tensions

43
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.360
offset improving supply from the
region, with the market weighing attacks

44
00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.480
against forecasts of a glut.

45
00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.080
OilPrice dot com notes that tanker-tracking
data still show Gulf outflows

46
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.560
below pre-war levels. An analysis
there argues that a shortage of empty

47
00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.760
tankers heading into the
Gulf could cap exports.

48
00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.640
Some traders are already
looking past the risk.

49
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.040
Bloomberg reported that major trading
houses are in talks with QatarEnergy

50
00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.680
for term supply next year, mostly the
Qatar Marine and Qatar Land grades.

51
00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.560
That rests on unnamed sources,
and QatarEnergy hasn't commented.

52
00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.800
Turning to Europe. The European
Parliament and member states agreed on

53
00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.720
Thursday to push back the
methane regulation by two years.

54
00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.080
Without the delay, importers would
have had to document methane emissions

55
00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.960
on imported oil and gas
from the start of next year,

56
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.560
according to Rigzone. Importers had
warned they couldn't find enough

57
00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:17.040
compliant supply in a tight market,
and OilPrice dot com also reports

58
00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.800
pressure from the US, Europe's
biggest oil and gas supplier.

59
00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.040
In practice, American LNG and crude
keep flowing into Europe without

60
00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:28.000
a new layer of paperwork
and verification cost.

61
00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.280
That matters while gas
storage is still drawing down.

62
00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:34.960
Separately, Bloomberg has seen a
Commission draft that would require

63
00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.480
member states to match their emergency
oil reserves to national fuel

64
00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.600
consumption and refining capacity.

65
00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:44.400
It follows a war that showed crude
in storage doesn't guarantee enough

66
00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.480
diesel or jet fuel. This is only
a draft and hasn't been adopted.

67
00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:52.960
If it goes through, holding stocks by
product could add to European demand

68
00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.080
for middle distillates.

69
00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.040
Over in Asia, India imported a
record amount of crude in October.

70
00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.360
According to Reuters trade data,
imports reached nearly five point six

71
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.520
million barrels a day. That's up
four point seven percent on September

72
00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.320
and six point nine
percent on a year earlier.

73
00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:14.000
Saudi volumes hit an eight-month
high as Gulf shipments recovered.

74
00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:17.920
Those barrels are adding to Russian
supply in India rather than replacing

75
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.400
it. Russia stayed India's largest
supplier at one point eight five million

76
00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.520
barrels a day, up three point
five percent on the month.

77
00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:27.280
A few more things.

78
00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.360
A court ruling threatens the licence
for Sentinel Midstream's two point

79
00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.880
one billion dollar deepwater
crude export project off Texas.

80
00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.640
That account comes from the environmental
group that petitioned the court,

81
00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:41.120
and no response from
Sentinel has been reported.

82
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.920
The leaders of the US, China and Russia
agreed to boost global fuel supply,

83
00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:49.360
according to Rigzone. No
volumes or timing were given.

84
00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.920
In the Black Sea, the security firm
Ambrey says ships may be targeted

85
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.160
for past calls at Ukrainian ports, even
when the current voyage has nothing

86
00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:59.400
to do with Ukraine.

87
00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:03.400
Brazil's crude output hit a record
four point seven million barrels a

88
00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.360
day in September. That's up twenty
point three percent on the year,

89
00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.120
with more of it heading to Europe.

90
00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:13.600
Venture Global and China Gas have
expanded their long-term LNG agreement.

91
00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:15.440
Volumes weren't disclosed.

92
00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:19.600
And in the Permian, Presidio is buying
Rushmore's Southern Midland assets

93
00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.320
for three hundred and
sixty million dollars.

94
00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.840
The deal adds about twelve thousand
eight hundred barrels of oil equivalent

95
00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:26.600
a day.

96
00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:30.800
What to watch next. Gas Infrastructure
Europe's daily storage readings

97
00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:33.360
run through to the
twenty-sixth of November.

98
00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:37.680
Then on Wednesday, the EIA's weekly
report covers the week to the twentieth,

99
00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.600
including distillate stocks.

100
00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.200
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
